# Resume Project — Cursor Rules

## Project overview

This repository contains LaTeX CVs for **Marouane Dbibih** (DevOps & Cloud Engineer). CVs are **single-page, A4, French-first**, with a modern sober design and ATS-friendly structure.

## Repository structure

```
resume/
├── MASTER_CV.md              # Master source of truth (do not invent content absent from here)
├── data.json                 # Generic CV data
├── resume.tex                # Generic template (layout, macros, style)
├── resume-data.tex           # Generic CV content
├── resume.pdf
└── devops-and-cloud/
    ├── devops-and-cloud-fr.json   # French DevOps/Cloud CV data (primary source)
    ├── devops-and-cloud-en.json   # English DevOps/Cloud CV data
    ├── devops-and-cloud.tex       # DevOps template (layout, macros, photo, style)
    ├── devops-and-cloud-data.tex  # DevOps content (regenerate from JSON)
    ├── devops-and-cloud.pdf
    └── profile.png                # Circular headshot (top-right of header)
```

## Workflow

1. **Edit JSON first** (`devops-and-cloud-fr.json` or `devops-and-cloud-en.json`) for content changes.
2. **Regenerate** the matching `*-data.tex` from JSON.
3. **Do not edit** `*.tex` templates for day-to-day content updates — only for layout/style changes.
4. **Compile** after changes:
   ```bash
   cd devops-and-cloud && latexmk -pdf devops-and-cloud.tex
   ```
5. **Clean aux files**: `latexmk -c`

Engine: **pdflatex** only (`% !TEX program = pdflatex`).

## Content rules (strict)

- **Never invent** experiences, projects, certifications, metrics, or employers not present in `MASTER_CV.md` or the active JSON file.
- **Do not re-add** removed content (e.g. OCP Group experience) unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Do not add fake numbers** (uptime %, VM counts, time savings) without user confirmation.
- Certifications keep their **official English titles**.
- Job titles stay in **English** (e.g. `DevOps & Cloud Engineer`, `DevSecOps Engineer`).

## Language conventions

### French CV (`devops-and-cloud-fr.json` → French PDF)

- **Translate to French**: summary, section titles, project/experience descriptions, skill category labels, languages, interests.
- **Keep in English**: tool names, cloud services, technologies, ATS keywords, certification names, GitOps/CI/CD/DevSecOps terms, product names (Flippix, Scrappix, Nuriko, AsemMokllati).

### Section titles (French DevOps CV)

Use separate sections — do **not** merge:

- Résumé professionnel
- Compétences techniques
- Expériences professionnelles
- Projets
- Certifications
- Langues
- Centres d'intérêt

## Skills section

- **One row per JSON category** — do not merge categories unless the user asks or space absolutely requires it (prefer keeping them split).
- **French category labels**, **English technology values**.
- Map JSON keys to labels:
  - `plateformes_cloud` → Plateformes cloud
  - `conteneurisation` → Conteneurisation
  - `iac_et_automatisation` → IaC & automatisation
  - `cicd` → CI/CD
  - `devsecops` → DevSecOps
  - `observabilite` → Observabilité
  - `reseaux` → Réseaux
  - `virtualisation` → Virtualisation
  - `systemes_exploitation` → Systèmes d'exploitation
  - `registres_et_stockage` → Registres & stockage
  - `bases_de_donnees` → Bases de données
  - `gestion_de_versions` → Gestion de versions
  - `developpement` → Développement

## Experience section

Format per entry (`\cvExperience` — 5 args):

1. Company (bold)
2. Position (bold)
3. Period — French format: `Oct. 2025 -- Présent`, `Mars 2025 -- Août 2025`, `Juil. 2024 -- Août 2024`
4. **Projet :** — one short French sentence
5. **Technologies :** — comma-separated list (English)

No separate "Réalisations" block unless added to JSON.

## Projects section

Format per entry (`\cvProject` — 3 args):

1. **Title** (bold)
2. **Description** — **1–2 lines maximum**, prose only
3. **Technologies :** — comma-separated list (English)

### Project description rules

- **No bullet lists** (`\textbullet`, dashes, or inline lists).
- **No technology names in the description** — tools/stacks go **only** under Technologies.
- **Flippix / Nuriko**: description must focus on **DevOps & Cloud work** (infra, K3s, IaC, Helm, GitOps, CI/CD, observability, platform ops) — not product/analytics features (ROI, SP-API, seller analytics).
- **AsemMokllati / Azure K3s**: focus on platform engineering (HA cluster, GitOps, CI/CD, storage, TLS, observability, day-2 ops).
- Keep descriptions concise to fit **one page**.

## Header & contact

- **Left-aligned** text; **circular photo top-right**.
- Photo: `profile.png`, **cover-style crop** (fill the circle, no white gaps), ~2.6 cm diameter, thin primary-color border.
- Contact line includes:
  - Location: `Casablanca, Maroc`
  - Phone: `+212 6 15 55 44 45`
  - Email: `marouane@dbibih.com`
  - LinkedIn: `linkedin.com/in/marouanedbibih`
  - GitHub: `github.com/marouanedbibih`
  - GitLab: `gitlab.com/marouanedbibih`

## LaTeX design system

- Class: `extarticle` 9pt, A4
- Font: Inter → Source Sans Pro → Helvetica (fallback chain)
- Colors: primary `#003366`, secondary `#1F3A5F`
- `\linespread{1.06}` — readable spacing; target **1 page** (adjust spacing before merging content)
- Margins: 1.2 cm left/right, 0.9 cm top/bottom
- Company names and job titles: **bold** (not italic)
- No tables, no footer/header fields, no images except profile photo

## ATS guidelines (when optimizing)

- Use recognizable section names (French or English — be consistent per CV variant).
- Prefer date formats: `MM/YYYY` or `Mois YYYY -- Mois YYYY`.
- Include measurable results only when verified with the user.
- Keep `ats_keywords` in JSON in English; do not remove them.
- Scan scores depend on matching the **target job** — a DevOps CV will score low against unrelated roles (e.g. Data Analyst).

## JSON schema conventions

When adding/updating entries in `devops-and-cloud-fr.json`:

```json
{
  "personal_information": { "full_name", "job_title", "location", "phone", "email", "linkedin", "github", "gitlab" },
  "summary": "...",
  "skills": { "<category_key>": ["tech1", "tech2"] },
  "experience": [{ "company", "position", "period", "project", "technologies" }],
  "projects": [{ "name", "alias?", "role?", "published?", "description", "highlights?", "technologies", "links?" }],
  "certifications": [{ "name", "code?" }],
  "languages": [{ "name", "level" }],
  "interests": ["..."],
  "ats_keywords": ["..."]
}
```

After JSON edits, sync `devops-and-cloud-data.tex` and recompile.

## What to avoid

- Do not commit unless the user asks.
- Do not create README or docs files unless requested.
- Do not merge skill categories without user approval.
- Do not duplicate technologies in project descriptions.
- Do not use centered header (left-aligned only).
- Do not stretch the CV beyond 1 page without telling the user.
- Do not use `keepaspectratio` letterboxing for the profile photo — always fill the circle.

## Compilation prerequisites

```bash
sudo apt install texlive-latex-extra texlive-fonts-extra texlive-lang-french latexmk
```
